            <ArticleTitle>Duodenal diverticula: potential complications and common imaging pitfalls.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>1072-6</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.1016/j.crad.2014.05.103</ELocationID>
            <ELocationID EIdType="pii" ValidYN="Y">S0009-9260(14)00286-4</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>A duodenal diverticulum is a commonly encountered entity in gastrointestinal radiology with a wide variety of appearances. The purpose of this review is to describe the normal anatomy and embryology of the duodenum, discuss the differences between a true versus intraluminal duodenal diverticulum, and to highlight the normal appearance, potential complications, and imaging pitfalls of duodenal diverticula.</AbstractText>
